{"step_index":96,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T20:08:07Z","thinking":"**Constructing DTOs**\n\nI've got the repositories all set, which means I can move on to the next step. I'm now crafting the Data Transfer Object (DTO) classes in the backend. I'm starting with `AuthRequest`, `RegisterRequest`, and `AuthResponse`, and `UserDto` definitions. I'll need these classes for data exchange between the client and server.\n\n\n**Defining More DTOs**\n\nI've moved on to fleshing out more DTOs. Now I'm focused on the `UserProfileDto`, building on the `UserDto` and adding rating history, counts, and stats. I'm also working on `ProblemDto` which needs detailed fields for descriptions, constraints, and code. Then I have `TestCaseDto`, a basic but important definition for test cases. Finally, I'm defining the matchmaking and submission-related DTOs.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"package com.codeduel.dto;\n\nimport java.time.LocalDateTime;\n\npublic class ApiResponse<T> {\n    private boolean success;\n    private String message;\n    private T data;\n    private String code;\n    private LocalDateTime timestamp;\n\n    public ApiResponse() {\n        this.timestamp = LocalDateTime.now();\n    }\n\n    public ApiResponse(boolean success, String message, T data, String code) {\n        this.success = success;\n        this.message = message;\n        this.data = data;\n        this.code = code;\n        this.timestamp = LocalDateTime.now();\n    }\n\n    public static <T> ApiResponse<T> ok(T data) {\n        return new ApiResponse<>(true, \"Operation successful\", data, \"OK\");\n    }\n\n    public static <T> ApiResponse<T> ok(String message, T data) {\n        return new ApiResponse<>(true, message, data, \"OK\");\n    }\n\n    public static <T> ApiResponse<T> error(String message, String code) {\n        return new ApiResponse<>(false, message, null, code);\n    }\n\n    // Getters and Setters\n    public boolean isSuccess() { return success; }\n    public void setSuccess(boolean success) { this.success = success; }\n\n    public String getMessage() { return message; }\n    public void setMessage(String message) { this.message = message; }\n\n    public T getData() { return data; }\n    public void setData(T data) { this.data = data; }\n\n    public String getCode() { return code; }\n    public void setCode(String code) { this.code = code; }\n\n    public LocalDateTime getTimestamp() { return timestamp; }\n    public void setTimestamp(LocalDateTime timestamp) { this.timestamp = timestamp; }\n}\n","Description":"Standard ApiResponse DTO","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\codeduel\\backend\\src\\main\\java\\com\\codeduel\\dto\\ApiResponse.java","toolAction":"Creating ApiResponse.java","toolSummary":"Write ApiResponse DTO"}}]}
